<title>MEXICO: Vector sells CoreStates exchange house stake.</title>
<headline>Vector sells CoreStates exchange house stake.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican brokerage Vector announced Wednesday the sale of a 20 percent stake of Vectodivisas, its exchange house subsidiary, to U.S.-based CoreStates Financial Corp</p>
<p>The acquisition was made through Philadephia Equities International, a CoreStates subsidiary, Vector said in a statement. Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>((-- Daniel Perez-Whitaker, Monterrey bureau +528 3457617))</p>
</text>
